ccupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{3}{8}Mr\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}M{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{4}{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}M({\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}M\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta (1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -\\frac{{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta }{3}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12M}{5}(1-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{8M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379909 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379910 13194139536027 true] [17592186379909 1089 "q-163576" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379909 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536027 true] [17592186379909 1100 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." 13194139536027 true] [17592186379909 1113 #uuid "42754aea-7d8d-54b5-837e-0461d25b662a" 13194139