The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{4}{9\\pi }M{r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9\\pi }M{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{9\\pi }({\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2\\pi }\\cdot ({\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\theta )}{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2\\pi }\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}\\theta -\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\theta ]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2\\pi }\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379932 13194139536027 true] [17592186379931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379933 13194139536027 true] [17592186379931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379934 13194139536027 true] [17592186379931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379935 13194139536027 true] [17592186379931 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379936 13194139536027 true] [17592186379931 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536027 true] [17592186379931 1041 "selection" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379931 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379935 13194139536027 true] [17592186379931 1110 #uuid "85e903b2-e31d-50b2-afca-dfb20dadf9b2" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379932 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379932 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536027 true] [17592186379932 1111 #uuid "4dc8c3d1-413d-544b-9266-8cc15bf82ccc" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379933 1034 "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379933 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536027 true] [17592186379933 1111 #uuid "53086998-2c28-53ca-9caa-cf03493be237" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379934 1034 "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379934 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536027 true] [17592186379934 1111 #uuid "552ec8db-ab66-5495-912a-a61bbcf5c11b" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379935 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379935 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536027 true] [17592186379935 1111 #uuid "629729fa-bbe3-5f4a-960b-a75563f95ecb" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379936 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379936 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536027 true] [17592186379936 1111 #uuid "6fea5c47-7dca-52ef-80db-584acd1cd454" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379937 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379938 13194139536027 true] [17592186379937 1089 "q-163600" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379937 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536027 true] [17592186379937 1100 "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the curve $y=\\sqrt{x},$ the line $y=1,$ and the $y$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=12Mxy.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." 13194139536027 true] [17592186379937 1113 #uuid "1b75f6b7-1feb-5cd3-b6ce-f7c0075a6bc6" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379937 1145 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,\\sqrt{x}\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot 12Mxy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{1}{x}^{3}y+x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}x{y}^{4}]}_{y=\\sqrt{x}}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}x)-(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}x+\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12M{[\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{4}-\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =12M(\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{1}{16}-\\frac{1}{10}) \\\\  & =12M\\cdot \\frac{7}{80} \\\\  & =\\frac{21M}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{21M}{20}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{21}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379939 13194139536027 true] [17592186379938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379940 13194139536027 true] [17592186379938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379941 13194139536027 true] [17592186379938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379942 13194139536027 true] [17592186379938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379943 13194139536027 true] [17592186379938 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536027 true] [17592186379938 1041 "selection" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379938 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379942 13194139536027 true] [17592186379938 1110 #uuid "0d8f84ea-33ea-5ed0-8e57-33764b41f2fa" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379939 1034 "\\frac{4}{5}" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379939 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536027 true] [17592186379939 1111 #uuid "63216723-86dd-5ed7-b0c3-effa279969ad" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379940 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4}" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379940 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536027 true] [17592186379940 1111 #uuid "3eb0cefe-1946-5d9f-8d93-4684d174f423" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379941 1034 "2\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" 13194139536027 true] [17592186379941 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536027 true] [17592186379941 1111 #uuid "d20cdaab-47a4-5b36-8b23-0d8606eb9626" 13194139536027 true] [1759218637